Subject: [PATCH] subsystem_restart: a subsystem may restart on its own

As ../kernel/patches/0025 for 3.10. Every Qualcomm subsystem starts with the
restart level SYSTEM: if one crashes, the whole tablet restarts. Stock set the
modem's to RELATED from user space, so that a modem crash cost the mobile
connection for a few seconds. A device tree property, read when the subsystem
registers, does the same here; the board marks the modem with it.
---
--- drivers/soc/qcom/subsystem_restart.c
+++ drivers/soc/qcom/subsystem_restart.c
@@ -1802,6 +1802,13 @@
 		if (!subsys->desc->edge)
 			pr_debug("Reading qcom,edge for %s failed\n",
 								desc->name);
+
+		/*
+		 * A subsystem marked so in the device tree restarts on its own when
+		 * it crashes, instead of taking the whole system down with it.
+		 */
+		if (of_property_read_bool(ofnode, "qcom,restart-level-related"))
+			subsys->restart_level = RESET_SUBSYS_COUPLED;
 	}
 
 	ret = sysmon_notifier_register(desc);
